WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.840
What is the One Piece? What happened during&nbsp;
the void century? And how will One PIEce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.160
the possibly most well-written&nbsp;
story of our time, end?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.400
These are the 3 biggest questions&nbsp;
that every One piece fan is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.560
burning to get the answers to above anything else.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.520
And every now and then a theory comes&nbsp;
around, an idea so wild and different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.400
that no matter how unlikely it might be&nbsp;
to actually turn out to be the truth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.160
it completely turns our perspective&nbsp;
on One Piece completely on its head.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.400
This is one of these ideas, that has a very&nbsp;
unconventional and radical take on the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.240
twist on Luffy's adventure to become the king&nbsp;
of the pirates and change the world. Why?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:52.720
Because it involves one of the, if not the most&nbsp;
controversial tropes of storytelling: Time Travel.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.560
And yet, even though I am usually very sceptical&nbsp;
of this concept myself, if what I'm about to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:07.360
you is true, it would make for the most satisfying&nbsp;
ending to One PIece, that I have yet come across.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.560
Based on the most recents developments in&nbsp;
the [SPOILER WARNING] we all have taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.520
it for granted, that Luffy is Joyboy.&nbsp;
Whether that means that he is possessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:21.600
has awakened his spirit or simply has inherited&nbsp;
his will, many people were quite sceptical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.160
about the idea that Luffy might stop being only&nbsp;
Luffy, but become a child of prophecy, who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:36.400
destined to do great things right from the start.&nbsp;
Luffy being some sort of reincarnation might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.960
take away from his achievements and&nbsp;
being the special and unique person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:48.000
who we all have grown to love and cheer for over&nbsp;
many many years. All now thrown overboard with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.040
the reveal that Luffy is JoyBoy, the man Roger&nbsp;
and Oden and Manny others have been waiting for.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:01.440
But what if we got it all wrong. What if it's&nbsp;
one of Eichiro Oda's famous red herrings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.800
Like how teach said he didn't have that type of&nbsp;
ambition to become the second division commander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.720
because of course he had much&nbsp;
greater ambitions than that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:17.280
Or how the Gomu Gomu no mi was a mythical&nbsp;
Zoan fruit all along. So what if Luffy wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:24.800
really JoyBoy. What if Joy Boy was actually&nbsp;
Luffy, who traveled back to the void century.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.120
Sounds absolutely ridiculous at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.960
but you might be surprised how well this&nbsp;
would fit into the storyline overall.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.720
So even if I wouldn't rate it as&nbsp;
the most probable thing to happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.320
I'm sure you will enjoy the conclusion to this.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.200
It all started with a message I got a few weeks&nbsp;
ago from a mysterious subscriber of this channel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:53.840
who shared with me a number of articles and posts&nbsp;
about the idea that the strange world of One PIece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:03:00.000
might be the result of a time loop or time leap&nbsp;
happening. Most of these ideas were basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.960
pure fan fiction. However a few ideas stood&nbsp;
out to me as quite interesting at that point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.160
For instance, how certain events seem to repeat&nbsp;
themselves throughout history. The government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:18.400
that has apparently conducted major cleansings&nbsp;
throughout the centuries. People like Joy Boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:24.160
Noland or Roger repeatedly popping up in different&nbsp;
eras. How the void century and people of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:30.160
past keep communicating with the present through&nbsp;
objects like the poneglyphs or inherited will. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:37.360
of course the parallel between Luffy's straw hat&nbsp;
and the giant straw hat on Marijoe, kept by Imu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:44.160
the secret ruler of the world, who looks like a&nbsp;
giant hand of a clock sitting on their throne.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.960
And in general, as you know, time shenanigans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.920
and always have been a very very&nbsp;
popular theme in Anime and manga.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.560
The thing that finally got my full attention&nbsp;
on this idea however, was a 2 year old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:05.360
video by a smaller One Piece YouTuber called&nbsp;
'Otherwise ace' who published a video titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:12.000
'Luffy is the Original Joyboy from the Void&nbsp;
Century', long before Zunisha recognised Luffy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.960
awakening as JoyBoy. Shoutout to him. I'll&nbsp;
leave a link to it in the description below.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:23.680
In his video he gives a bunch of wonderful&nbsp;
evidence, how Luffy and the straw hats travelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:30.880
back to the void century would fit in surprisingly&nbsp;
well with the story up to now. And given what we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:37.840
know about Luffy and his devil fruit, I think&nbsp;
this has all become just the more fascinating.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.520
Before we talk about how Luffy and&nbsp;
co would even get into the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.000
let's just assume they do for now.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.800
The most interesting and mysterious clue&nbsp;
about Laugh Tale and the One Pice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.840
we have gotten in the story so far is&nbsp;
the Roger pirates arriving there and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.120
literally bursting into laughter, most&nbsp;
likely after reading Joy Boys story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:05.600
as Roger himself comments that he would have loved&nbsp;
to meet JoyBoy and live in the same era as him.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.680
Well if LUffy were Joy Boy, that would mean&nbsp;
that Roger was actually reading the story of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:21.840
straw hats, that we have been reading up to this&nbsp;
point as well. A story that is meant to bring us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.560
joy with all its adventures and a quirky&nbsp;
crew and Luffy being the person who will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:32.560
change the world by going back in time. It&nbsp;
would also be hilarious to Roger and co,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:37.680
because not only would they be reading the best&nbsp;
story ever, but also follow the adventures of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.440
someone who will be born 20 years later. And&nbsp;
they themselves will be included in the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.960
written on the poneglyphs as well. They will&nbsp;
all know about how they themselves helped Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.880
reach his goal. Pretty meta I know, but&nbsp;
let's be real how awesome would that be.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.760
Luffy would tell where he was from and about&nbsp;
his brother ace and how his death would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:05.280
the key to becoming pirate king. Suddenly,&nbsp;
Roger decides to have a kid, that he then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:12.400
entrusts to none other than Garp, the man who he&nbsp;
fought by side by side and Luffy's Grandfather.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.680
It would also change the line of Roger&nbsp;
wishing he had been born in JoyBoy's era and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:24.720
Rayleigh saying that they were too early. That&nbsp;
would all make sense if they were talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:27.920
Luffy's era. Roger knew he would die and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:35.520
never meet him. And it's also why they knew&nbsp;
exactly about the 20 years until his return.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:41.520
It of course also fits in nicely with Oden's&nbsp;
prediction of JoyBoy returning and opening the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:47.840
borders of Wano, which of course has now actually&nbsp;
happened. Zuneshia was the one who confirmed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:55.600
his old companion had returned, and who better to&nbsp;
make friends with a giant elephant, than Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:02.240
who we have seen befriending all types of giant&nbsp;
animals throughout the story. The kraken serum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.680
the bull on dressrosa, the&nbsp;
animals during his time skip.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.920
Now obviously, as you will already&nbsp;
have noticed by this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:18.080
this idea gets really messy really fast. Like,&nbsp;
who influences what? Who actually changes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:25.360
future or is everyone just caught in a time&nbsp;
loop? How can Luffy change the present, if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:31.360
he is part of the past? Telling such&nbsp;
a story is a real walk on the edge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:37.520
but if there is one person I would trust&nbsp;
in pulling it off, it's Eiichiro Oda.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.360
One major issue with this idea, that&nbsp;
'OtherwiseAce' mentions with this theory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:46.080
is the fact, that Buggy, Crocus, Shanks&nbsp;
and Rayleigh, all members of the Roger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.920
pirates didn't recognise Luffy as JoyBoy.&nbsp;
Interstingly enough however, we do know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:59.280
that it was exactly those 3, Shanks, Buggy and&nbsp;
Crocus, that stayed behind as the ROger pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:05.760
traveled to the final island. They were the&nbsp;
only 3 who never got to read the entire story.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.520
On top of that, I personally think&nbsp;
that for Shanks and Crocus you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:15.760
very well argue that they DID in fact recognise&nbsp;
Luffy. As I've talked about a bunch before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:24.240
Shanks basically bet everything on Luffy becoming&nbsp;
the person Roger had been waiting for. Similarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.320
Crocus wonders if Luffy is that&nbsp;
same man they're waiting for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:34.640
implying that Roger was waiting for&nbsp;
Joyboy, who we now know IS in fact Luffy.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:41.520
And Rayleigh, who DID go to Laugh Tale, has&nbsp;
been acting very suspiciously around Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:46.240
right from the start. The very first&nbsp;
words he tells Luffy is that he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.800
wanted to meet him, the very same&nbsp;
words ROger used on Laugh tale.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.480
He even offers Luffy to tell&nbsp;
him the secret of Laugh tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:01.840
already knowing that Luffy would refuse&nbsp;
and then goes on to train him personally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:09.040
for 2 years. Rayleigh know&nbsp;
exactly that Luffy is Joy Boy.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.200
Actually looking at it from this lens&nbsp;
makes all of Luffy's interactions with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.320
Rayleigh pure goosebump moments for me.&nbsp;
Like when Rayleigh asks Luffy whether he&nbsp;&nbsp;

